).\n- Grounding: final program == baseline AMIP+prefix exact-refit search; verified top-1 drop fractions Arena 0.046%, MT-Bench human 2.7%, GPT-4 6.0%, NBA 0.9%; ~16x smaller than random (log2 ~3.98). Knapsack variants untested (infra OSError), so excluded from queries.\n- Rejected: title-like 'leaderboard stability' queries (forbidden-paper risk), generic benchmarking/optimization filler, variant-name/chronology queries.\n{\"timestamp\": \"2026-10-29T00:40:00Z\", \"step\": \"implement\", \"scope\": \"attempt\", \"attempt_id\": \"c03_seeded_prune_relinearized_knapsack_attempt_01\", \"idea_id\": \"c03_seeded_prune_relinearized_knapsack\", \"program_id\": \"program_1\", \"summary\": \"Implemented baseline-seeded exact pruning plus relinearized category knapsack in program_1/src/program.py. Components: _baseline_amip (the starter fallback); _build_categories/_stats_from_counts (p x p count refits); _prune_baseline_seed + _prune_counts (phase 1, 40% of cap: binary search plus single-unit exact pruning); _candidate_pairs + _relinearized_greedy (phase 2: damped 0.65 relinearized knapsack over 2-6 boundary pairs); _swap_refine (phase 3: 2-for-1 swaps); _verify_rows (row-level warm+cold refit, 1e-6*(1+|tol|) safety; must be strictly smaller than the starter). The integer cap comes from _deterministic_refit_cap; the wall clock is only a 0.85*deadline backstop; exceptions fall back to the starter set.\", \"files_changed\": [\"program_1/src/program.py\"], \"evidence\": \"not executed (stage rules forbid local runs); rubric source patterns confirmed by grep; program_spec.toml identical to program_0\", \"next_action\": \"harness evaluation; inspect diagnostics search_error, verify_failures, final_size vs baseline_size, chosen_source\", \"tags\": [\"gate=pending\"]}\n{\"timestamp\": \"2026-10-28T23:45:29Z\", \"step\": \"reference_query_plan\", \"scope\": \"paper\", \"summary\": \"Reference query plan written: 9 component-literature queries (AMIP, influence/IJ, BT MLE, top-K ranki