** one NBA game changes the top-5 in both seasons. On MT-Bench, the GPT-4-judge ranking needs more drops than the human one to change the leader (143 vs 92) but fewer to change the top 3 (150 vs 229).\n\nAll sizes are verified upper bounds, not proven minimums, and differences between designs are descriptive rather than causal.\n\n**Plan**\n- **Figures:** three, all full width because the ICLR template is single-column (5.5 in text width):\n  - an overview diagram;\n  - the size in counts and as a share of the data, side by side;\n  - the human-vs-GPT-4 comparison plus a chart of how the dataset ordering changes between counts and shares.\n- **Appendix:** per-case and per-seed tables, full definitions, the unsupported superiority test, the unscored variants, reproducibility details, and the LLM Usage section ICLR requires.\n\n**Things the writer needs to handle**\n- **Citations:** `references.bib` is mostly off-topic search noise. Only `Broderick2020AnAF`, `Giordano2019AHS`, `Monari2000WithdrawingAE` (and optionally `Alaa2020DiscriminativeJQ`) are usable. Key background papers from the task brief, such as Bradley–Terry and Chatbot Arena, are missing and have to be added through the reference step before they can be cited.\n- **Dataset sizes:** the per-dataset comparison counts (e.g. 135,622 for Arena) aren't reported directly. I worked them out by dividing each verified count by its reported share, and the paper needs to say that.\n- **Uncertainty:** there are no confidence intervals from resampling the data. The only interval available is the one for the ratio against random drops, so this has to be listed as a limitation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5805,"cache_read_input_tokens":108167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5805},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"in